Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||12-17-2000||08:41 AM||||I'm thinking of doing some body mods beginning in May. I have a Gold 1986 2m4 that I'd like to put a GT nose on. How much should I expect to pay if I bought the nose myself and took to a dealer to install?<P>Also, do the TRW Blade rims have a gold center or would I have to paint those myself?<P>TIA!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mi Junk||12-17-2000||08:59 AM||||You also need a bunch of brackets and a rad plate. I did a swap a couple of years ago w/ a brand new nose. It cost me around $500 Cdn.<BR>Oh BTW you have to change or mod. the inner fender wells.<BR> I think a dealer will charge through the NOSE. hehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||Tigger||12-17-2000||03:33 PM||||There's also a 5mph impact egg crate plastic piece behind the cover too.  I think you may have to cut your old one down if you can't find the one made for the aero bumper.<P>Prices roughly range anywhere $150 to $200 depending on condition and whether all the needed brackets are included.<P>I agree, a dealer will probably want big $$$ to do the job.  You may have better luck at a local bodyshop, they might charge you less.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
